Upstream attribution
====================

This project is a HarmonyOS (OpenHarmony) port of an existing Android
application and is built on a third-party USB/IP server library. Neither the
USB/IP protocol implementation nor the USB device handling originates here.

Upstream application
--------------------

  yunsmall/Android-Usbipdcpp
  https://github.com/yunsmall/Android-Usbipdcpp

  An Android USB/IP server app, licensed GPL-3.0. This HarmonyOS port follows
  its architecture, its user-facing feature set (start server / bind device /
  live log viewer) and its Node-API bridge layout. The original Android
  implementation remains the work of its author and contributors.

USB/IP server library
---------------------

  usbipdcpp
  https://github.com/yunsmall/usbipdcpp
  Licensed under LGPLv3.

  This product uses usbipdcpp (https://github.com/yunsmall/usbipdcpp),
  licensed under LGPLv3.

  usbipdcpp is statically linked into libusbip_napi.so. In accordance with
  LGPLv3 section 4, the complete corresponding source of this application is
  published in this repository, and every change applied to usbipdcpp is kept
  in patches/usbipdcpp-ohos.patch so that the library can be rebuilt and
  relinked against a modified version.

Other third-party components
----------------------------

  libusb 1.0.30         LGPL-2.1   https://github.com/libusb/libusb
  Asio                  BSL-1.0    https://github.com/chriskohlhoff/asio
  spdlog (bundled fmt)  MIT        https://github.com/gabime/spdlog

The HarmonyOS module skeleton (build scripts, hvigor files, ContinuousTask
scaffolding) was started from an application template and has been rewritten
for this project.

